in this video we're gonna be talking  about what tariffs are how they work and  how Trump's tariffs are going to in  already are affecting Apple have you  ever wondered why Apple devices like  iPhones and Mac books cost more in other  countries around the world like Germany  Mexico or India  well that's because those countries  imposed tariffs on goods from other  countries like China and the USA let's  say India imposes a 10% tariff on China  and a consumer in India decides to buy a  $1000 iPhone which is manufactured in  China the consumer would have to pay  $1100 for the iPhone with the extra $100  going to the Indian government this move  is good for India for a couple of  reasons first off it'll help bring in  extra revenue but much more importantly  it'll encourage companies to manufacture  their products inside of India  so that Indian consumers don't have to  pay those tariffs now here's the kicker  that's exactly what Apple is doing right  now  Apple supplier company wished Iran has  already been making the iPhone SC in  iPhone 6s from within India for a couple  of years now completely avoiding the  import tariffs on those iPhone models  being purchased by Indian consumers this  is great for both India and Apple  because it provides jobs for Indian  citizens boosting the Indian economy and  it means more iPhone sales for Apple  since Indian consumers can more easily  afford them  now that the tariffs are out of the way  and this leads us into the us-china  trade war and how Apple got stuck in the  middle for years even before he became  president of the United States Donald  Trump has been complaining about China  and their unfair practices like in 2011  when Trump said that China exported more  goods to the US than they purchased  which he claimed was unfair because it's  better for their economy and worse for  ours for example a report came out in  2014 claiming that the United States  lost 32 million jobs since 2001 due to  outsourcing to China so why were we  outsourcing to China  well because labor wages in the other  costs and China are many times cheaper  than wages in the United States Apple  has been doing this for years and  selling their devices virtually  tariff-free this was great for both  Apple and China so they've now got a  flood of new factories in their country  filled with Chinese workers boosting  their economy even though labor rates  were that low  however it wasn't so good for the US  since all those factories could have  been made in the United States and bring  thousands of jobs ever says Trump was  elected in 2016  he's been trying to get US companies to  come back and invest here in a number of  ways one way that seems to have worked  is lowering taxes on offshore profit  brought back into the United States from  35% down to 15% which basically meant  that if a u.s. corporation profited 1  billion dollars in China they would have  to pay 350 million dollars to the US  government just to bring that money back  into the US and spend it here with the  offshore tax now down companies  substance brought back four times as  much money in one year six hundred sixty  five billion dollars in 2018 compared to  only 150 five billion dollars in 2017 an  apple alone will bring in and spend  three hundred and fifty billion dollars  over the next five years  thanks to that drop in the tax rate now  let's get to Trump's other tactic  tariffs and how they affect Apple just a  few days ago Trump announced a ten  percent tariff on virtually everything  that's imported from China including  Apple's iPhones and most other devices  and accessories and right after the  announcement Apple stock value dropped  by over five percent now if the tariffs  go through starting on September first  which is by the way only a couple of  weeks before they announce to 2019  iPhones then Apple will have a couple of  choices either they keep price is the  same and US consumers will end up paying  more for future iPhones or in the worst  case scenario switch to another  smartphone brand like Samsung because  iPhones are going to be more expensive  on the other hand Apple could take the  loss themselves lowering the price of  their iPhone so that we the consumers  will still end up paying the same amount  as before it's been estimated that if  Apple absorbs the tariffs their revenue  would fall by 4 percent in 2020 which  could translate into several billion  dollars of lost profits which is very  bad news for investors in the main  reason why their stock value dropped  over five percent after the announcement  if that's the case US consumers won't  really have much to worry about  since iPhone prices will stay the same  but either way tariffs are bad news for  Apple in one scenario their prices go up  and sales go down or in another prices  stay the same but profits go down so  what options does Apple have  well since we don't know if these  tariffs are going to be temporary or  long-term Apple should most likely just  absorb the terrace for now until we find  out what's going to happen in the long  term and if the us-china trade war keeps  escalating there's a chance that Apple  might end up leaving China and move its  factories elsewhere Trump would prefer  that Apple moves their manufacturing to  the United States but seeing as labor  rates are so high I don't see that  happening anytime soon  unless the US government offers Apple  some incentives Apple has actually tried  that in the past with the Mac Pro in  2013 investing over 100 million dollars  to kick-start US manufacturing in Austin  Texas but it ended up not working out  because of higher labor rates in the  lack of enough people with the skills  needed for modern manufacturing  processes which is thriving in China and  there's now the new 2019 Mac Pro coming  this fall and Apple has already  announced that it will in fact be  manufactured in China however Apple has  another option available if things don't  go well in China with the trade war and  that's India Apple already has two  factories making their products in India  the wished Iran plant in the Foxconn  plant which will begin mass production  of higher-end iPhone models this year  those existing plants will make it  easier for Apple to move the rest of  their production over to India if they  so choose along with lower labor rates  which are actually lower than the rates  in China and India is currently on pace  to overtake China as the world's most  populated country and has been booming  as far as tech now we're not sure which  path Apple's gonna take but for now  Apple is gonna have to deal with those  China tariffs on the plus-side  Apple services revenue has been  skyrocketing for the past few years  allowing them to fall back on that  instead of product sales which I've  recently been going down due to market  saturation if you enjoy this video make  sure to tap that like button and click  the circle above to subscribe and check  out that video to see why Apple MacBooks  are so expensive thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

